    "patchSets": [
        {
            "number": 1,
            "revision": "d8907ee2da022709ee9822228a3d2aafc765ba10",
            "parents": [
                "0e78828ce927548b4dd679e06fdaf2f294983289"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/44/77944/1",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "aishwaryjoshi31",
                "email": "aishwaryjoshi31@gmail.com",
                "username": "aishwaryjoshi31"
            },
            "createdOn": 1738668389,
            "author": {
                "name": "aishwaryjoshi31",
                "email": "aishwaryjoshi31@gmail.com",
                "username": "aishwaryjoshi31"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Location.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "You know about these?\n\nyaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Connector/Embedded.interface"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Location.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "aishwaryjoshi31",
                        "email": "aishwaryjoshi31@gmail.com",
                        "username": "aishwaryjoshi31"
                    },
                    "message": "As per my understanding Connector/Embedded interface would make more sense for a port. What about representing location for other components like a processor ?\n\nFYI this PDI is required to add support for LocationType property. This PDI can be used generically for representing location of various devices (Processor, Chassis, Storage Device etc).\nEg usage for Processor through https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/77960"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Location.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "aishwaryjoshi31",
                        "email": "aishwaryjoshi31@gmail.com",
                        "username": "aishwaryjoshi31"
                    },
                    "message": "@patrick@stwcx.xyz any feedback on this ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Location.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't know why we would put a location on an element itself when we could put it on the connector.\n\nWe have other connectors than just 'Embedded', which is the only one you responded to.  Other applications already implement these connector types (see estoraged and smbios-mdr).  We're not going to do it different just because you want to.\n\n> FYI this PDI is required to add support for LocationType property. \n\nNo... it isn't required to add that functionality.  You've chosen a particular implementation and maybe this interface meets _your_ chosen implementation, but that doesn't mean we're accepting it as is.\n\nThe BMC is not a Redfish engine.  Just because there is a Redfish property somewhere doesn't mean we're going to model it exactly that way."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Location.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "@aishwaryjoshi31@gmail.com I agree with Patrick - we should make these empty interfaces under Connector as opposed to adding them here. That makes these interfaces more generic/usable/ and also implmentable on a need basis.\n\n@patrick@stwcx.xyz I wonder if we should document guidelines to help new contributors to this repo under https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/blob/master/requirements.md. I've noted several in the past from your reviews and I see some of them as comments on Aishwary's patches as well. Let me know if that makes sense to you - I can update the documentation to propose guielines (or you could if you have a ready list)."
                }
            ],
